{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1356736-fair-entrance-2e-conversion","id":1356736,"title":"Fair Entrance 2e Conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-23T18:46:16-08:00","id":1356736,"title":"Fair Entrance 2e Conversion","content":"One of my favorite Goblin Contracts, Fair Entrance, didn't make the initial transition from 1e to 2e, so I thought I'd take a stab at reworking it according to the contract creation guidelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#00703c\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Fair Entrance</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#00703c\"><span style=\"font-family:Rackham, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Goblin)</span></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The changeling\u2019s natural affinity for escaping confinement is strengthened. The changeling can now attempt to open any door as easily as the owner, disarming </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">alarm systems and bypassing locks with ease. However, the character ensures that they will be left similarly vulnerable.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>1</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> Glamour</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dice Pool: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">None</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Action: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Instant</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration: </b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Instant</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Effects</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">The changeling gains a bonus equal to their Wyrd on the next Larceny roll they make to bypass a lock or alarm, requires no tools to do so, and suffers no penalty for being unskilled (if applicable). In addition, the character scores an Exceptional Success with three successes instead of five. If examined, the door or alarm will show signs of having been tampered with, and cameras and recording equipment will reveal the intrusion, unless the character scores an Exceptional Success on the roll.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Drawback</b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Goblin Debt from this contract draws unfriendly attention. The next time someone with hostile or malevolent attention tires a lock on a dwelling or vehicle regularly used by the character, The Storyteller may spend a point of the character\u2019s Goblin Debt to ensure that the lock is open and any alarm system fails to function (passive cameras are not affected). Using this Contract </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">multiple times before this debt is spent attracts people with malicious intent to the character\u2019s dwelling or vehicle and makes attempts to invade their space or steal from them more likely.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy Old Style, serif\"><b>Loophole: </b>The character carries an article of clothing or a photograph of someone who regularly unlocks the door.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Notes</b>: I figured that this was in line with the power of the other Goblin Contracts, enhancing the changleing's abilities of escape and allowing them to use it in a more hostile way. The drawback there was how I figured I could get the drawback of the original contract into the new rules (as the story potential of drawing nasty things to you was what drew me to this contract in the first place).<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T13:14:46-08:00","id":1356846,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Hostile Takeover common contract? It functions quite similarly but without the goblin drawbacks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T14:31:28-08:00","id":1356851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1356736-fair-entrance-2e-conversion?p=1356846#post1356846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you looked at the Hostile Takeover common contract? It functions quite similarly but without the goblin drawbacks</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Goes back and rereads Hostile Takeover.</i><br /> <br /> ...Well, damn. You're right. <i>*sigh*</i> <br /> <br /> One of the things I liked about Fair Entrance was the risk involved in using it, to be honest. It added an interesting and flavorful drawback that told a story, but yeah, Hostile Takeover is pretty much this but all upside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-24T18:47:59-08:00","id":1356873,"title":"","content":"I do somewhat miss first edition's unique drawbacks, but they were frequently too big of a stick for too small of a carrot. It did make the exceptions really feel special though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}